@startuml epathmap-serialization-pipeline
' ============================================================================
' PathMap report §5.2 — before → after: how an EPathMap reaches the wire.
'
' Diagram type: an ACTIVITY DIAGRAM with a split between the deleted BEFORE
' pipeline and the current AFTER pipeline, chosen because the improvement is a
' change of PROCESS SHAPE — a hereditary per-entry re-encode walk performed on
' every encode versus a memoized snapshot copied on every encode — and an
' activity diagram shows repetition and memoization boundaries directly.
'
' Colour convention — one hue per concept:
'   RED    #FFCDD2/#C62828  the deleted per-entry walk (before)
'   TEAL   #B2DFDB/#00695C  the cold path (first serialization)
'   GREEN  #C8E6C9/#2E7D32  the warm path (every later serialization)
'   PURPLE #E1BEE7/#6A1B9A  the generated stack-safe protobuf PDA
' ============================================================================
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.4
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #455A64
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor #455A64

title <b>Serialization pipeline, before → after</b>\nbefore: <latex>\Theta\!\left(\sum_{e\in m}|\mathrm{prost}(e)|\right)</latex> re-derived per encode · after: one cold build, then <latex>\Theta(|EPM1(m)|)</latex> memcpy

start
:`EPathMap` serialization requested;
split
  -> **BEFORE** — the tag-1 entry walk,\n**deleted by SS-C5** (`1b576c90`);
  :flatten the trie to a `repeated Par`
  list at **tag 1**;<<#FFCDD2>>
  :re-encode **each entry from scratch**,
  hereditarily through nested maps —
  on **every** encode AND every `encoded_len`;<<#FFCDD2>>
  :far side re-files the list,
  one `encode_trie_path` per entry,
  under prost's 100-level read budget
  (ceiling measured at 31–33 levels);<<#FFCDD2>>
  note right #FFEBEE
    ⚠ **No remaining caller.** The arm was
    deleted, not converted — removing the
    traversal removed both the per-encode
    walk and the inherited read ceiling.
  end note
  kill
split again
  -> **AFTER** — the EPM1 snapshot (SS-C9, `26876b65`);
  if (snapshot memoized?) then (no — **COLD**, once per clone family)
    :take PathMap's compact-tree accessor →
    **ACTree03 arena**, verbatim;<<#B2DFDB>>
    :enumerate map values in arena value order,
    encode each on the **generated protobuf PDA**
    (explicit work/value stacks — flat native stack);<<#E1BEE7>>
    :assemble EPM1 = magic · version · mode ·
    arena · value table, stored in
    `OnceLock<Vec<u8>>` on the `EntryTrie`;<<#B2DFDB>>
  else (yes — **WARM**)
  endif
  :**one memcpy** of the snapshot into the carrier:
  prost **field 9** (`bytes`) / bincode **first field**;<<#C8E6C9>>
  note right #E8F5E9
    ★ Shared by every clone of the trie: warm
    encode is <latex>\mathcal{O}(1)</latex> work before the
    caller's required copy — measured **20 ns**
    warm accessor at 1,024 entries.  A cached
    `EpmLayout` keeps only the topology prefix,
    so nested map-value chains do not retain
    <latex>\Theta(d^2)</latex> suffix bytes.
  end note
  stop
end split

legend bottom
  |= cell |= meaning |
  |<#FFCDD2>| the deleted hereditary per-entry walk |
  |<#B2DFDB>| cold path — first serialization of a clone family |
  |<#E1BEE7>| generated stack-safe protobuf PDA (value stream) |
  |<#C8E6C9>| warm path — memoized snapshot memcpy |
endlegend

@enduml
